<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus February CPI declines 1.55 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Cyprus February CPI declines 1.55 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyprus's consumer price index declined 1.55 percent in February to 116.24 units from 118.07 in January, the island's statistics and research department announced.</p>
<p>    Consumer price index	Feb 97   Jan 97   Feb 96</p>
<p>    Month/month change (pct)   -1.55    nil	-2.40</p>
<p>    Year/year change (pct)	3.55    2.66	2.74</p>
<p>    Index (92=100)		116.24   118.07    112.25</p>
<p>The department the decline was due to discount sales in clothing, footwear and furniture. Increases were noted in the prices of certain vegetables, local cheese and electricity.</p>
<p>-- Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
</text>
